      <div class="col-12 col-md-10">
	<div class="row">
	  <div class="col-sm-2">
            <h2 class="section-heading mb-0 bg-faded2 p-3 rounded">
              <span class="section-heading-upper tw">What is body or Yom</span>
            </h2>
	  </div>
	  <div class="col-sm-1"></div>
	  <div class="col-sm-7 bg-faded2 p-3 rounded">
            <p class="mb-0">Your body, or yom, is the base physicality of your existance. Head to toe, inside and out, every part of the physical being is considered. </p>
            <p class="mb-0">&nbsp</p>
            <p class="mb-0"></p>
            <p class="mb-0">&nbsp</p>
	  </div>
	</div inner-row>
	<div class="row p-3 tw"></div>
	<div class="row p-3 tw"></div>
	


	<div class="row p-2 tw">
	  <div class="col-sm-2">
            <h2 class="section-heading mb-0 bg-faded2 p-3 rounded">
              <span class="section-heading-upper tw">Style</span>
            </h2>
	  </div>
	  <div class="col-sm-1"></div>
	  <div class="col-sm-7 bg-faded2 p-3 rounded">
            <p class="mb-0">The core of the Yomonsni massage of body is about relaxation and induction of pleasure. This is achieved by drawing through a variety of massage techniques or schools, taking elements of stretching from the Thai or Yoga massage, long deep strokes drawing on elements of Swedish and Shiatsu (though generally without the bruising pressures that can be applied). Hands and feet are addressed with techniques loosely inspired by reflexology. Face and scalp are just worked lightly.</p>
            <p class="mb-0">&nbsp</p>
            <p class="mb-0"></p>
            <p class="mb-0">&nbsp</p>
            <p class="mb-0"></p>
            <p class="mb-0">&nbsp</p>
            <p class="mb-0"></p>
            <p class="mb-0">&nbsp</p>
	  </div>
	</div innerrow>
	<div class="row p-3 tw"></div>
	<div class="row p-3 tw"></div>
	
	
	
       
